{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PermInversion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PermInversion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Fin.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.exists_adjacent_descent_of_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.exists_adjacent_descent_of_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L160-L174","doc":"**`π ≠ 1 ⟹` there is an adjacent descent** `π (a+1) < π a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.eq_one_of_invCount_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.eq_one_of_invCount_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L145-L158","doc":"**`invCount π = 0 ⟹ π = 1`.**  No inversions means `π` is strictly monotone, hence the\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.strictMono_of_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.strictMono_of_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L118-L143","doc":"Increasing on every adjacent pair implies strictly monotone (general `n`, by induction on the\ngap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.eq_one_of_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.eq_one_of_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L109-L116","doc":"A strictly monotone permutation of `Fin n` is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.invCount_mul_swap_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.invCount_mul_swap_lt","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L55-L107","doc":"**Descent swap strictly lowers the inversion count.**  If `b = a + 1` and `π b < π a`\n(an adjacent descent), then `invCount (π * swap a b) < invCount π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.swap_lt_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.swap_lt_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L32-L53","doc":"An adjacent swap reverses the order of exactly the pair `(a, a+1)`; every other increasing pair\nstays increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.invCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.invCount","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PermInversion.lean#L28-L30","doc":"**Inversion count** of a permutation of `Fin n`: the number of pairs `i < j` with `π j < π i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}